<section class="policy">

  <h2>Who We Are</h2>
  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Black Stallions LP ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, shares, and protects information when you visit blackstallions.us, submit a form on this site, or respond to one of our ads on Facebook or Instagram (operated by Meta Platforms, Inc.).</p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <h3>Information You Provide Directly</h3>
  <p>When you fill out a form on this site, respond to a Facebook or Instagram Lead Ad, or contact us directly, we may collect: your name, phone number, email address, company name, equipment type (Box Truck, Power Only, or Flatbed), MC/DOT number, preferred lanes or regions, and any other details or message you include.</p>
  <h3>Information Collected Automatically</h3>
  <p>Like most websites, we and our advertising partners may use cookies, pixels, and similar tracking technologies to understand how visitors use this site and to measure and improve our ads. This includes the Meta Pixel, which allows Meta to help us measure ad performance, build audiences for retargeting, and deliver ads that may be more relevant to you based on your visit to this site.</p>

  <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your inquiry and match you with available freight or carrier partners</li>
    <li>To contact you about onboarding, including fuel card and ELD setup</li>
    <li>To follow up on quote requests from moving companies seeking backhaul freight</li>
    <li>To measure and improve the performance of our website and advertising, including ads run through Meta</li>
    <li>To build retargeting audiences so people who've shown interest may see relevant ads from us again</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where required by law, we rely on your consent or our legitimate business interest in operating and promoting our services as the basis for this use.</p>

  <h2>Information Shared With Meta and Other Third Parties</h2>
  <p>If you submit a Lead Ad form through Facebook or Instagram, Meta collects and processes the information you submit under its own <a href="https://www.facebook.com/policy.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Data Policy</a>, separate from this one. We receive the information you submit through that form and use it according to this Privacy Policy.</p>
  <p>We do not sell your information. We may share it with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Carrier partners, shippers, or freight partners, as needed to fulfill a placement or quote request</li>
    <li>Service providers such as fuel card or ELD vendors, as needed for onboarding</li>
    <li>Meta, through tools like the Meta Pixel and Lead Ads, for ad delivery, measurement, and retargeting</li>
    <li>Other service providers who help us operate this site or communicate with you (such as email or CRM tools)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your Choices</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the information we hold about you, or to stop contacting you, at any time using the contact details below. We will respond within a reasonable timeframe, consistent with applicable law.</p>
  <p>You can also control how Meta uses your information for ads directly through Meta's own tools, including <a href="https://www.facebook.com/adpreferences/ad_settings" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook Ad Preferences</a>, or through general advertising opt-outs at <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutads.info/choices</a> or, in the EU, <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</p>

  <h2>Data Retention</h2>
  <p>We retain your information for as long as needed to respond to your inquiry and, if you become a partner or placement, for the duration of that relationship plus any period required for recordkeeping or legal compliance. Analytics and advertising data is generally retained for up to 24 months unless deleted sooner at your request.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable steps to protect the information you share with us, but no method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>This site and our services are intended for business use by adults. We do not knowingly collect information from children, and our forms are not directed at anyone under 18.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or legal requirements. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or your information? Reach us at:<br>
  Phone: 315-953-6939<br>
  Email: Business@blackstallions.us</p>
